From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Ling <ling_kasim@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dsi: don't round byte clock before reparenting to the PLL

dsi_calc_clk_rate_6g() rounds the computed byte clock through
clk_round_rate() while the byte_src RCG is still parented to the TCXO.
clk_byte2_determine_rate() derives the achievable rate from the *current*
parent, so for a DSC panel that needs 72.77 MHz it returns the TCXO-derived
38.4 MHz instead.  That value is then used both for the PHY timing
(byte_clk_rate * 8) and for dev_pm_opp_set_rate(), which programs the DSI
PLL VCO for the wrong byte clock.

The source clock is only reparented to the DSI PHY PLL later, in
dsi_link_clk_set_rate_6g_v2_9().  Once the PLL is the parent the rounding is
harmless; before that it corrupts the rate.  The v2 path
(dsi_calc_clk_rate_v2) does not round at all, and clk_set_rate() rounds to an
achievable rate on its own, so drop the premature rounding.

Fixes (on AYN Odin 3 / Chipone ICNA3520, 1080x1920@120 with 3:1 DSC):

  dsi_link_clk_set_rate_6g: Failed to set rate pixel clk, -22
  msm_dsi_host_power_on: failed to enable link clocks. ret=-22
  msm_dsi ae94000.dsi: Power on failed: -22
  panel-chipone-icna35xx ae94000.dsi.0: failed to initialize panel: -22

which leaves the DSI link down and the DPU command-mode encoder timing out.

Signed-off-by: Alex Ling <ling_kasim@hotmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 11 ----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -677,8 +677,6 @@ static void dsi_calc_pclk(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, bool is_bonded_dsi)
 
 int dsi_calc_clk_rate_6g(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, bool is_bonded_dsi)
 {
-	long rounded_byte_clk_rate;
-
 	if (!msm_host->mode) {
 		pr_err("%s: mode not set\n", __func__);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -686,15 +684,6 @@ int dsi_calc_clk_rate_6g(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host, bool is_bonded_dsi)
 
 	dsi_calc_pclk(msm_host, is_bonded_dsi);
 
-	rounded_byte_clk_rate = clk_round_rate(msm_host->byte_clk,
-					       msm_host->byte_clk_rate);
-	if (rounded_byte_clk_rate < 0) {
-		pr_err("%s: failed to round byte clock rate, %ld\n",
-		       __func__, rounded_byte_clk_rate);
-		return rounded_byte_clk_rate;
-	}
-
-	msm_host->byte_clk_rate = rounded_byte_clk_rate;
 	msm_host->esc_clk_rate = clk_get_rate(msm_host->esc_clk);
 	return 0;
 }
